<div class="mb-8">
  <Heading size="2xl" as="h1" class="mb-2">CheckBox</Heading>
  <Text size="lg" tone="subdued" as="h2">
    A toggle input for boolean values with an optional label, help text, and validation state.
  </Text>
</div>

<!-- Canonical example -->
<div class="mb-8">
  <Example source={'
    <CheckBox name="terms" label="Accept terms and conditions"/>
  '}/>
</div>

<!-- Usage -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Usage</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg bg-card overflow-hidden">
    <CodeBlock code={"<CheckBox name=\"terms\" label=\"I agree to the terms\"/>\n\n<CheckBox name=\"newsletter\" label=\"Subscribe\" checked/>\n\n<CheckBox name=\"agree\" label=\"I agree\" help=\"Required\" error=\"You must agree\"/>"}/>
  </div>
  <Prose class="mt-4">
    <p>
      A CheckBox is a self-contained form control. The <code>name</code> and <code>value</code>
      props map directly to the underlying <code>&lt;input type="checkbox"&gt;</code>. The
      <code>label</code> is automatically linked via a generated <code>id</code>, so clicking the
      label text toggles the checkbox.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- When to Use -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">When to Use</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      Use checkboxes when the user needs to toggle a single boolean option (like accepting terms),
      or select multiple items from a list of choices. Each checkbox operates independently — toggling
      one does not affect the others.
    </p>
    <p>
      For mutually exclusive choices where only one option can be selected, use radio buttons instead.
      For a simple on/off toggle with immediate effect (like enabling a feature), consider a switch
      component if available.
    </p>
    <p>
      Checkboxes belong in forms. For filtering or view options that take effect immediately without
      a submit button, a toggle or segmented control may be a better fit.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Behaviour -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Behaviour</Heading>
  <Prose>
    <p>
      The checkbox renders a hidden native <code>&lt;input&gt;</code> for form submission, overlaid
      with a custom styled indicator and check icon. This approach keeps native form behaviour
      (validation, serialization) while allowing full visual control.
    </p>
    <p>
      When an <code>error</code> is present, it replaces the <code>help</code> text — they never
      appear simultaneously. This avoids visual clutter and ensures the most important message
      (the error) is always visible.
    </p>
    <p>
      If no <code>label</code> is provided, the component falls back to a humanized version of
      the <code>name</code> prop (e.g. <code>accept_terms</code> becomes "Accept terms").
    </p>
  </Prose>
</div>

<!-- Examples -->
<div class="flex flex-col gap-12 mb-12">
  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">With Help Text</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Provide additional context below the checkbox to explain what the option does or why it
        matters.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <CheckBox name="newsletter" label="Subscribe to newsletter" help="We will send you updates once a week."/>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">With Error State</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Display a validation error when the field is required but unchecked. The error replaces
        the help text to keep the layout clean.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <CheckBox name="terms" label="Accept terms and conditions" error="You must accept the terms to continue"/>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Checked by Default</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Pre-select the checkbox using the <code>checked</code> attribute. Useful for opt-out
        patterns or settings that are enabled by default.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <CheckBox name="notifications" label="Enable notifications" checked/>
    '}/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Disabled</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Disabled checkboxes are visually muted and cannot be toggled. Use them to indicate that
        an option exists but is not currently available.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <CheckBox name="disabled_unchecked" label="Unchecked disabled" disabled/>
        <CheckBox name="disabled_checked" label="Checked disabled" checked disabled/>
      </div>
    '} align="start"/>
  </div>

  <div>
    <Heading size="md" as="h3" class="mb-2">Multiple Checkboxes</Heading>
    <Prose class="mb-4">
      <p>Group related checkboxes with the same <code>name[]</code> for multi-select scenarios.
        Each selected value is submitted as part of an array.</p>
    </Prose>
    <Example source={'
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <CheckBox name="features[]" value="dark_mode" label="Dark mode"/>
        <CheckBox name="features[]" value="notifications" label="Push notifications" checked/>
        <CheckBox name="features[]" value="analytics" label="Usage analytics"/>
      </div>
    '} align="start"/>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Best Practices -->
<div class="mb-12">
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">Best Practices</Heading>
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-green-500/30 bg-green-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-green-600">Do</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Use positive phrasing: "Enable notifications" not "Disable notifications".</li>
          <li>Provide help text for options whose effect isn't obvious from the label.</li>
          <li>Group related checkboxes visually and use a shared heading above them.</li>
          <li>Show validation errors inline, close to the checkbox they relate to.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
    <div class="border rounded-lg p-4 border-red-500/30 bg-red-500/5">
      <Heading size="sm" as="h4" class="mb-2 text-red-600">Don't</Heading>
      <Prose>
        <ul>
          <li>Use a single checkbox for mutually exclusive choices — use radio buttons.</li>
          <li>Pre-check options that sign the user up for something (newsletters, data sharing).</li>
          <li>Use double negatives: "Don't not send me emails" is confusing.</li>
          <li>Rely on the checkbox alone for critical confirmations — pair with a dialog or alert.</li>
        </ul>
      </Prose>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- API Reference -->
<div>
  <Heading size="lg" as="h2" class="mb-4">API Reference</Heading>
  <div class="border rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-muted">
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Prop</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Type</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Values</th>
          <th class="text-left px-4 py-2 font-medium">Default</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y">
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">name</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any string</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">value</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any string</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">"1"</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">label</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any string</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil (humanized name)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">help</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any string</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">error</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any string</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">checked</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Boolean</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">true, false</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">false</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">disabled</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Boolean</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">true, false</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">false</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">id</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">String</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2">Any string</td>
          <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">nil (auto-generated)</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
